  "summary": "The traditional craft of forging bronze and brass instruments for gamelan orchestras, particularly gongs and metallophones.",
  "description": "Gamelan smithing involves the precise casting and hammering of bronze alloys to create instruments with specific tonal qualities, using techniques like cire perdue (lost-wax casting) and cold-hammering. The craft combines metallurgical knowledge with musical understanding, as each instrument must be tuned to the specific pelog or slendro scales used in Javanese and Balinese music.",
